          .standout
            %p This entry is about the text
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A Survey of Elliptic Cohomology
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Algebraic Topology
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.harvard.edu/~lurie/papers/survey.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-01200-6_9"} doi:10.1007/978-3-642-01200-6_9
            %p It
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  reviews basics of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+cohomology"} elliptic cohomology
              %li
                %p
                  indicates the construction of the
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
              %li
                %p
                  and discusses this in the context of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+cohomology"} equivariant cohomology
            %p The central theorem is
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the realization of the moduli space of
                  = succeed "s" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curve"} elliptic curve
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structured+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} structured (∞,1)-topos
              %li
                %p
                  with a structure
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaf"} (∞,1)-sheaf
                  of
                  = succeed "-valued" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+ring"} E-∞ ring
              %li
                %p
                  such that the
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+ring"} E-∞ ring
                  of global sections of this structure sheaf.
          %p
            See also
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Elliptic+Cohomology+I"} Elliptic Cohomology I
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chromatic+Homotopy+Theory"} Chromatic Homotopy Theory
          %h1#table_of_contents Table of Contents
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#Summary"} Summary
              %p The following entry has some paragraphs that summarize central ideas.
              %ol
                %li
